!! What it does

''kind streams'' lets a single [[Streams|$:/plugins/sq/streams]] node carry a [[kind|$:/plugins/rimir/kind]] type. Once typed, the node is visually marked in the outline and its kind fields become editable in place — without opening the node as a separate tiddler.

Three affordances:

* ''Identify'' — a collapsed pill shows the node's `kind.type` key; a left accent marks the row.
* ''Edit'' — expanding the pill renders kind's `stream-view` field bar for that node (lazily).
* ''Assign'' — right-click → ''Kind type ▸'' opens a flyout submenu (styled like the Streams menu) listing the kind types.

!! How it hooks in

Streams renders each node's content through `$:/plugins/sq/streams/templates/stream-row-body`, which is a bare `<$transclude mode="block"/>` — it does //not// pass through `$:/core/ui/ViewTemplate`, so kind's ViewTemplate-attached field bar never appears inside the outline.

This plugin ships its own copy of that template with a `plugin-priority: 2` (Streams is `1`), so TiddlyWiki's shadow-precedence rules make this copy win. The override adds a cheap gate: only nodes with a `kind.type` render the extra component.

!! Performance model

|!Node state |!Cost |
|Untyped |one `has[kind.type]` test; renders nothing |
|Typed, collapsed |one pill (single field read) + an unopened `<$reveal>` |
|Typed, expanded |full `stream-view` field bar — only for opened nodes |
|Assigning |submenu in the context menu; type list renders only when the flyout opens |

!! Reuse

No field-rendering or type logic is duplicated: the expanded bar transcludes kind's `stream-view`, and the assign submenu reuses kind's type filter (top-level types in the active namespace), rendered with Streams' own menu markup.

